    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">Can You Choose the Route on a Private Boat Trip in Madeira?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>25 December 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">Partly. Chifbay&#x27;s two trips follow set routes west along the south coast, but on a private boat you can ask for more time at one stop, less at another or a stop dropped, and the skipper agrees when the sea and the return time allow. A completely different route is a custom trip, arranged on WhatsApp.</p>

      <h2>What are the two set routes?</h2><p>Both trips leave Marina do Funchal and head west, with the cliffs on your right. They share the same first stretch of coast and differ in how far they go and what happens on the way.</p><p>The <a href="/hidden-coves-half-day">Day Trip west of Funchal</a> runs in this order:</p><ol><li><strong>Funchal's waterfront.</strong> Out of the marina and along the city's sea front, past the Lido and the long pebble beach of Praia Formosa.</li><li><strong>Câmara de Lobos.</strong> The fishing town with its painted boats, seen from the bay.</li><li><strong>Cabo Girão.</strong> The great sea cliff, 580 metres high, where the drone is launched on days the wind is kind.</li><li><strong>Fajã dos Padres.</strong> The main stop: a swim, jumps from the boat and the paddle boards, below terraces that no road reaches.</li><li><strong>Ribeira Brava.</strong> A second swim off the town at the mouth of its valley.</li><li><strong>Ponta do Sol.</strong> On the 3 hour option only, about 30 minutes further west.</li><li><strong>The run home.</strong> A fast, straight ride back to Funchal.</li></ol><p>The <a href="/sunset-cruise">Sunset Trip along the cliffs</a> is simpler. It follows the same coast with no swimming, and turns back at Cabo Girão on the 2 hour option or at Ribeira Brava on the 2h30.</p><h2>What can you ask to change on the day?</h2><p>The balance between the stops. On a private boat your group decides what matters most, and the skipper shapes the time around it when conditions allow.</p><p>Requests that work well:</p><ul><li><strong>A longer swim at Fajã dos Padres</strong>, with less time at Ribeira Brava, for a group that came to swim and jump.</li><li><strong>No second swim</strong>, and more time drifting under Cabo Girão for photos, for a group that is cold or simply happy on deck.</li><li><strong>A slow pass in front of Câmara de Lobos</strong>, for anyone who wants a good look at the harbour and its boats.</li><li><strong>A quieter corner</strong> for a nervous swimmer or a child, even if it is not the most famous spot.</li><li><strong>A slower ride home</strong>, if the fast run is not for someone in your group.</li></ul><p>Say it early. The right moment is on the pontoon or in the first ten minutes, not just as the boat turns for home. A request made at the start can be built into the whole trip. One made at the end can only be squeezed in.</p><h2>What stays fixed?</h2><p>Four things do not change, however nicely you ask.</p><h3>The return time</h3><p>Each option has a set length. A Day Trip leaving at 10:00 is back at 12:30 or 13:00, one leaving at 14:00 is back at 16:30 or 17:00, and the Sunset Trip lasts 2h or 2h30. Extra time in one place comes out of another.</p><h3>The direction</h3><p>Both trips go west. The coast east of Funchal, towards Garajau and on to Ponta de São Lourenço, is a different trip entirely. Our page on <a href="/posts/east-or-west-boat-trip-from-funchal">going east or west from Funchal</a> compares the two.</p><h3>No swimming on the Sunset Trip</h3><p>It is built around the evening light, and by then the water has lost the warmth of the day. If you want to swim, book the Day Trip.</p><h3>Safety</h3><p>Chifbay's terms say the skipper decides the route on the day, based on the sea, the wind and safety. That sentence settles any disagreement before it starts.</p><h2>Why does the sea get the final say?</h2><p>Because the same bay can be perfect one morning and wrong the next. Madeira's south coast is usually sheltered, but swell arriving from the south west or west can roll into bays that are flat on most days, and a breeze funnelling down a valley can make one stop choppy while the next is calm.</p><p>So the skipper may swap the order of the stops, choose a different corner of the same bay, or cut a swim short. None of that means your request was ignored. It means the skipper found the version of it that works in that day's water. Our page on <a href="/posts/how-the-skipper-chooses-the-swim-stop">how the skipper chooses the swim stop</a> walks through that thinking. On a day when the whole coast is wrong, the trip does not go out, and you take either a new date or a full refund.</p><h2>Which trip gives you the most freedom?</h2><p>The 3 hour Day Trip. Half an hour more is not a lot on paper, but it is the difference between a long swim at Fajã dos Padres and a rushed one, or between seeing Ponta do Sol and not. If your group knows it wants to linger, that extra time is where the flexibility lives.</p><p>The 2h30 option still leaves room to move things around, just less of it. On the Sunset Trip the main choice is distance: the turn at Cabo Girão or the longer run to Ribeira Brava.</p><h2>Can you plan a completely different route?</h2><p>Ask us on WhatsApp. Trips at other hours are set up there, and that is also where to ask about anything outside the two set routes. Explain what you have in mind, and we will tell you honestly what is possible and what is not. Do not book a set trip expecting it to turn into something else on the day.</p><p>If what you really want is time on land, a beach or a village, read <a href="/posts/can-you-go-ashore-on-a-private-boat-trip-in-madeira">whether you can go ashore on a private boat trip</a> before you write.</p><h2>How do you get the trip you want?</h2><p>Tell us your priorities, not a timetable. "We want as long as possible in the water" or "my father is nervous on the fast ride" gives the skipper something to work with. A minute by minute plan for a stretch of Atlantic does not.</p><p>Mention it when you book or in a WhatsApp message beforehand, then say it once more on the pontoon. The pages for the <a href="/cabo-girao-boat-tour">Cabo Girão boat tour</a> and the <a href="/faja-dos-padres-boat-trip">Fajã dos Padres boat trip</a> show the two places most groups want more of.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Can we skip the swim stops on the Day Trip?</h3><p>Yes, you can ask, and spend that time elsewhere on the route if the sea allows. Tell the skipper at the start of the trip.</p><h3>Does the Sunset Trip go further than Ribeira Brava?</h3><p>No. The 2 hour option turns at Cabo Girão and the 2h30 option at Ribeira Brava.</p><h3>Can the trip start somewhere other than Funchal?</h3><p>The set trips always start at Marina do Funchal. Ask on WhatsApp about anything else.</p><h3>Who has the last word on the route?</h3><p>The skipper, who decides on the day based on the sea, the wind and safety.</p>

      <blockquote>Tell the skipper what matters before Câmara de Lobos, not after Ribeira Brava.</blockquote>
    </article>
